        <description>
            Tortugas Mountain Observatory (TMO) is located on Tortugas Mountain, also known as “A” Mountain, 
            just east of Las Cruces and is managed by the Department of Astronomy at New Mexico State University. The observatory 
            is equipped with a 1967 Boller and Chivens 24″ reflector telescope. For decades the observatory was used primarily 
            for imaging and monitoring of planetary targets such as Jupiter, in support of NASA’s Voyager space probes. 
